<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      Theme for RearActivity, taken from another rear-panel app that has never
      exhibited the failure this fixes.

      THE SYMPTOM: locking the device made the rear panel's override appear on the
      FRONT screen, over the keyguard.

      THE CAUSE was the previous theme, Theme.Material.NoActionBar.Fullscreen: an
      OPAQUE fullscreen activity. RearActivity holds FLAG_SHOW_WHEN_LOCKED (it must —
      that is what keeps the panel alive through a lock), and when the keyguard comes
      up the system looks for a top opaque fullscreen activity to show over it. An
      opaque activity is exactly that candidate; a translucent one is not, so it is
      never hoisted onto the primary display in the first place.

      windowAnimationStyle=@null matters for the same reason and is not cosmetic: the
      default window animations run this window through the system's lock/unlock
      transition, which is itself a path by which it gets drawn on display 0.
      RearActivity's overridePendingTransition(0, 0) only covers its own launch, not
      system-driven transitions.

      Translucency costs nothing visually here: RearDialView.onDraw opens with
      canvas.drawColor(Panel.Palette.BG), so the view paints its own opaque background
      across the whole surface. Nothing shows through.
    -->
    <style name="RearTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.Translucent.NoTitleBar.Fullscreen">
        <item name="android:windowAnimationStyle">@null</item>
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@android:color/transparent</item>
        <item name="android:windowIsTranslucent">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
